<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The one entitlement a signed build asks for: the domain whose https sign-in handoff this
  app may receive.

  Approved by Tadas on 2026-09-13 (AGENTS.md, "The phone signs in through the web sign-in").

  **The service is `webcredentials`, not `applinks`, and the difference is the whole
  feature.** An https callback to `ASWebAuthenticationSession` is not a universal link: it
  is verified through the shared-web-credentials service, and a session asked for one on a
  domain this app only claims under `applinks` refuses to start, with "Using HTTPS callbacks
  requires Associated Domains using the webcredentials service type". `applinks` is
  deliberately absent as well as insufficient — it would route every tap on
  `/app/signed-in` anywhere on the phone into an app that has no handler for it, which is a
  launch into nothing. Apple verifies either by fetching
  /.well-known/apple-app-site-association from the host, which is what stops another app
  claiming a Motet sign-in — the weakness a custom URL scheme cannot close.

  **Deliberately not Motet.entitlements**, which asks for `com.apple.developer.carplay-audio`.
  That one is granted by Apple's manual review, and an ungranted entitlement fails a build to
  *sign* rather than merely lacking the feature. These two must stay in separate files until
  CarPlay is granted.

  The domain is a build setting rather than a literal: this repo is public and names no
  deployment's hosts. `ios/bin/testflight upload` passes it from the `testflight`
  environment's MOTET_IOS_APP_DOMAIN, and a build without that setting must not point
  CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS here — `webcredentials:` with nothing after it is not a domain.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>webcredentials:$(MOTET_APP_LINK_DOMAIN)</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
